# Keep build scripts and makefiles LF everywhere.  The Windows CI job checks
# the tree out on a Windows runner; a CRLF-converted shell script or Makefile
# would break the MSYS2 build, so these paths must always check out as LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
Makefile.* text eol=lf
*.mk text eol=lf
Rules.make text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
# C/C++ sources also stay LF: backslash-newline splices do not survive
# CRLF checkouts (backslash-CR-LF does not splice), so LF everywhere
# keeps Windows checkouts compiling the same bytes Linux does.
*.c text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.hpp text eol=lf
*.hrp text eol=lf
*.inl text eol=lf
